  "rewrite_sql": "SET lock_timeout = '2s';
SET statement_timeout = '30s';

-- Add CHECK constraint without validating (quick, catalog-only)
ALTER TABLE users ADD CONSTRAINT users_full_name_not_null CHECK (full_name IS NOT NULL) NOT VALID;

-- Validate the constraint (ShareUpdateExclusiveLock - allows reads/writes during scan)
ALTER TABLE users VALIDATE CONSTRAINT users_full_name_not_null;

-- Set NOT NULL (fast in PG16 since validated constraint exists)
ALTER TABLE users ALTER COLUMN full_name SET NOT NULL;

-- Drop the now-redundant check constraint
ALTER TABLE users DROP CONSTRAINT users_full_name_not_null;",
  "notes": "Replaced direct SET NOT NULL (which takes AccessExclusiveLock and blocks all access) with the safe pattern for PG12+: (1) ADD CONSTRAINT CHECK IS NOT NULL NOT VALID (fast, no scan), (2) VALIDATE CONSTRAINT (ShareUpdateExclusiveLock, scans table but allows SELECT/INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE), (3) SET NOT NULL (fast catalog update when validated constraint exists), (4) DROP redundant constraint. Added lock_timeout=2s to fail fast if blocked, and statement_timeout=30s to prevent indefinite hangs. If the column contains NULL values, VALIDATE will fail with a constraint violation - same as the original migration, but with safer locking that doesn't block all table access during the scan.",
